  "text": "Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line. Common to everything in the universe, motion, motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run, sleeping, air moves into and out of our lungs. Blood flows in arteries and veins, carry people, automobiles, and planes. Water flowing down a dam, leaves falling from trees. Earth rotates once every 24 hours, revolves round the sun once in a year. The sun in motion, in the Milky Way, Milky Way, moving within its local group of galaxies. Rectilinear motion, uniform acceleration, a set of simple equations, the Latin nature of motion, the Latin velocity. Point objects valid so far, as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations, size neglected without much error. Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line.",
